# Caddy reverse proxy in front of the Snapsbrew Docker stack.
#
# The web container answers plain HTTP on 127.0.0.1:8080 (APP_PORT). Caddy
# gets a certificate, terminates TLS and sends the original Host header and
# the X-Forwarded-* headers by default.
#
# 1. Replace snapsbrew.example with the host of APP_URL.
# 2. Copy this file to /etc/caddy/Caddyfile.
# 3. Run: systemctl reload caddy
# 4. Set TRUSTED_PROXIES in .env to the gateway address of the Docker network.

snapsbrew.example {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8080
}
